<title>USA: Country World to be dismissed from Chapter 11.</title>
<headline>Country World to be dismissed from Chapter 11.</headline>
<dateline>BALA CYNWYD, Pa. 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Holly Holdings Inc said on Thursday that the United States Bankruptcy Court, District of Colorado, had signed a dismissal order for the company's Country World Casino Inc unit to be dismissed from its Chapter 11 Bankruptcy case.</p>
<p>The company said that as of March 13, the unit has paid all its creditors in full and is in final negotiations to secure financing to build its planned parking structure, casino and hotel complex on its property in Black Hawk, Colo.</p>
<p>Holly Holdings is majority owner of Denver, Colo.-based Country World Casinos.</p>
</text>
